# This file ships with the boilerplate because the boilerplate becomes the
# project root, so it is in place before the first agent writes anything.
#
# This is a signing appliance. The secret inventory below is not generic
# hygiene — it is the product's threat model expressed as ignore rules
# (SZ-SEC-005: secrets never in logs, audit payloads, command-line arguments,
# URLs, browser storage, source control, or telemetry). Source control is in
# that list, and this file is the only thing enforcing it.

# ── Dependencies and build output ───────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
target/
**/target/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── Test and capture output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.profraw

# ── Key material and secrets. These are the lines that matter ───────────────
# HSM PINs, SO-PINs, DKEK shares and wrapped key blobs (SZ-HSM-*, SZ-SEC-001).
# A DKEK share in a git history is a recoverable signing key, and deleting the
# file later does not remove it from the history.
*.pin
*.dkek
*.wrapped
dkek-share*
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
!**/*.pub
secrets/
state/

# ── Runtime and environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/*.yaml
!config/*.example.yaml
!config/os-operations.yaml
*.log
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── Local and OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER ignore these. Each looks like generated or local state and is not:
#
#   spec/           The requirement register every review cites and the 17
#                   domain specifications. The register is the product.
#   contracts/      The ownership map that makes parallel work safe.
#   docs/           The operator and integration documentation the appliance
#                   ships with — an appliance whose runbook is not in the
#                   repository has no runbook.
#   packaging/, systemd/   The nftables, AppArmor, nginx and unit files that
#                   are the hardening (SZ-OS-*). They are configuration, not
#                   build output, and regenerating them by hand is how a
#                   hardened appliance quietly stops being hardened.
#   config/*.example.yaml, .env.example   The templates. They carry no secret
#                   by construction and they are how an operator starts.
#   **/*.pub        Public keys are meant to be committed. Note the asymmetry
#                   above: *.key is excluded, *.pub is re-included. A blanket
#                   rule on "keys" takes both halves and breaks verification
#                   while protecting nothing.
#
# scripts/check-boilerplate.sh fails if any of them is ignored.
